natomy objects such as a  sword and they can use the body of  another living being as a vessel but  they cannot take a physical form of  their own the goddess clan is mostly  made up of female beings but like the  demon clan and their ten commandments  the goddesses also have their own  special elite force known as the four  Archangels the four Archangels are  powerful angelic figures who unlike the  other members of the goddess clan appear  to be male members of the goddess clan  can be distinguished by their large  angel  wings and their appearance was clearly  inspired by the angels of the Bible  members of the goddess clan are known  for a number of unique abilities  including the power to heal the ability  to fly and the ability to purge and  destroy Dark Souls such as the souls of  demons in general the goddess clan  possesses a variety of abilities that  are especially effective in fighting  against demons and now let's move on to  the minor races the groups that are  either subcategories of one of the  larger races or clans or groups that  don't fit into any of the other  categories mentioned but are relatively  few in numbers so they are not  considered a major force in the world of  the seven deadly sins first up we have  the beast men not those guys this guy  beast men are creatures who have a  humanoid body but the head of an animal  and they may also have claws fur and  other animalistic features to put it  simply they are a mixture of beasts and  men hence the name beast men the only  beast man that we really got to know in  any significant way in the story so far  is Shivaji a fox man or where Fox who  essentially raised bond when bond was  young jeeva go was shown to be capable  of transforming into a human on command  even though that is not his true form so  we can speculate that perhaps like the  fairies all Beast men have the ability  to change their appearance in order to  look like humans the beast men have  strong animalistic abilities and  instincts which makes sense since they  are part beasts however they appear to  have been driven to the brink of  extinction by humans historically humans  have feared the beast men and seen them  as monsters kind of like the stories of  evil werewolves in our own world  aside from Chicago who is a fox man or  where Fox the other beast men have been  mentioned in the story include juegos  son also aware Fox and a Wolf Man or  werewolf that meliodas and Liz were sent  to hunt down once in the past then we  have the vampires yes the world of the  seven deadly sins also has vampires the  vampire  were allied with the demon clan during  the holy war and because of this some  believe that vampires are just another  type of demon but the vampires are  actually a separate minor race in the  world of the seven deadly sins and they  are not technically part of the demon  clan vampires look a lot like humans but  they also have sharp fangs and they are  able to turn humans into vampires by  biting them the humans that they turn  will then be compelled to serve them the  vampires feed on human blood but as a  race they are stronger than humans and  have a much longer lifespan next up are  the druids  the druids are human but they are a  unique group of humans that live in  isolation from other humans deep inside  the forest  the Druids look like normal humans  although many of them tend to have  silver hair or white hair  the Druids worship the goddess clan and  they considered a demon clan to be their  natural enemy  unlike most ordinary humans the Druids  are much more in touch with nature with  animals and with the spirit world and  they are able to perform magical spells  and techniques that normal humans cannot  these spells include the ability to heal  as well as the power to destroy dark and  corrupt souls such as the souls of  demons which are all techniques that  they share with the goddess clan it is  believed that these techniques were  taught to the druids  by the goddess clan as a reward for  their devotion to the goddesses and  finally we have the category that I will  refer to as other because it includes  hybrid artificial and unknown races some  characters from the seven deadly sins do  not really fit into any of the  categories that we talked about so far  these characters include gold third the  goat sin of lust who is an artificially  created doll and bond who used to be  human but became immortal after drinking  from the Fountain of Youth  now most of you probably know who this  next character is but just in case you  don't I won't name  but the fact is that in the seven deadly  sins there is also a character who is  the reincarnation of a goddess but is  currently in the body of a human druid  because of this this characters magical  powers are much greater than the powers  of a regular druid finally the race of  merlin de Bourgh sin of gluttony is  still unknown what we do know about  Merlin is that Merlin is not her true  name but just an alias that she uses  because her true name cannot be  pronounced by humans she was born in  beli a Lowen a city once known as the  capital of the Wizards and her birth  immediately attracted attention because  she was born with an amazing magical  power known as infinity the city of  Valhalla Wayne and the Wizards that  lived there were neutral during the holy  war but due to her unprecedented power  the warring goddess and demon clans both  tried to get Merlin to come over to  their side and they each offered secret  magical knowledge in return for her  support rather than picking either side  Merlin took the knowledge offered by  both sides angry that they've been  tricked the rulers of the goddess and  demon clans destroyed the entire city of  beli eluate but Merlin managed to escape  the destruction and she became the only  known survivor from the capital of the  Wizards now the question is is Merlin a  member of some separate wizard race a  race that was neutral during the  conflict and that is why her name cannot  be pronounced by humans because she is  not human but a member of this wizard  race perhaps after the destruction of  beli Alwyn this wizard race was  virtually destroyed along with the city  and that explains why we don't know more  about them they are essentially a lost  and forgotten race that's one option  but perhaps Merlin is just a really  special human or druid that was born  with an incredible power kind of like  esken or or maybe Merlin is somehow a  mix of different powerful races or  something else entirely we can't be sure  at this point  but that's what makes the world of the  seven deadly sins so unique there are so  many different and interesting races and  clans and yet there are still a ton of  mysteries and unknowns surrounding all  of them let me know down in the comments  what you think Merlin's true race is and  also don't forget to let me know which  race or clan you would want to be a part  of if you have the choice if you enjoy  the seven deadly sins content on this  channel be sure to leave a like to let  me know and if you are new don't forget  to subscribe and hit that notification  bell make sure you vote in the Twitter  poll for what type of seven deadly sins  content you want to see on this channel  in the future you can follow us on  Twitter and Instagram at anime uproar as  always thank you all so much for  watching your support really does mean a  lot and until next time see us space  cowboys  [Music]  you  [Music]
 

